'''Watto's junkshop''',<ref name="CL2016">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> also known as '''Watto's junkyard''',<ref name="Card Trader">{{SWCT|set=Base Series 1|cardname=C-3PO - Protocol Droid (TPM)}}</ref> was a [[junk dealer]]ship owned by the [[Toydarian]] [[Watto]]<ref name="TPM" /> on the outskirts of the huge [[Mos Espa]] city<ref name="World Building">{{InsiderCite|227|World Building (Star Wars Insider 227)}}</ref> of [[Tatooine]]. His [[Slavery|slave]], [[Anakin Skywalker]], worked in the shop by repairing salvage for his owner. [[Jedi Master]] [[Qui-Gon Jinn]] sought to purchase a [[T-14 hyperdrive generator]] at Watto's shop after becoming stranded on the [[planet]], but Watto refused to accept his [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] [[credit chip]]s. Eventually, Jinn [[Gambling|bet]] on Skywalker winning the [[Boonta Eve Classic]] [[Podracing|podrace]] to get the [[hyperdrive]] generator, and for the boy's freedom.<ref name="TPM" />

{{Struct-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
According to "[[World Building (Star Wars Insider 227)|World Building]]," Watto's junkshop was presumably part of the "[[upper sprawl]]" of Mos Espa established by ''[[Star Wars: The Book of Boba Fett]]''.<ref name="World Building" />

